leetgo
------
https://github.com/j178/leetgo
Copyright (c) 2022 Jo
MIT License

The per-language test drivers under `internal/runner/drivers/` are adapted
from leetgo's, and the comparator knowledge behind `internal/runner/overrides.go`
came from reading it. D-005 records why the drivers were vendored rather than
imported: importing `leetgo/lang` compiled 144 extra packages, including a
JavaScript interpreter and a second SQLite driver, none of which serve local
code execution.

The Python and Go drivers are direct adaptations. The C++ driver is a rewrite
as a single header, so it needs no build system. The JavaScript driver is new —
leetgo has none — but follows the same contract so the two behave identically
from Go's side.

